#### 3.3.1 World latent status aggregation.

The per-camera scene tokens Q^scene\hat{Q}\_{\text{scene}} only capture isolated view-specific information, which is insufficient for holistic world modeling. To enable effective future prediction and trajectory planning, we aggregate these tokens and integrate with ego status to construct unified frame-wise world status representations. The ego status across consecutive frames, which include driving commands, velocity, and acceleration, is encoded by an ego status encoder (a single-layer MLP) into ego status embeddings Sego∈ℝT×DlS\_{\text{ego}}\in\mathbb{R}^{\textbf{T}\times D\_{l}}. The scene tokens Q^scene\hat{Q}\_{\text{scene}} from the SCWE and the ego status embeddings SegoS\_{\text{ego}} collectively constitute the frame-wise world latent state.

