### 3.5 Training and Inference

Training Objective. Following prior work, we employ L1L\_{1} loss ℒt​r​a​j\mathcal{L}\_{traj} to optimize the generated multi-candidate trajectories by imitating expert trajectories. Geometric alignment computes cosine similarity loss ℒa​l​i​g​n\mathcal{L}\_{align} on normalized features, maximizing cosine similarity to distill spatial understanding capability. For the world model, we use MSE loss ℒw​m\mathcal{L}\_{wm} to optimize the prediction of future world state. Future ego status requires supervision over driving command, velocity, and acceleration, including ℒc​m​d=CrossEntropy​(Cp​r​e​d,Cg​t)\mathcal{L}\_{cmd}=\text{CrossEntropy}(C\_{pred},C\_{gt}), ℒv=MSE​(Vp​r​e​d,Vg​t)\mathcal{L}\_{v}=\text{MSE}(V\_{pred},V\_{gt}) and ℒa=MSE​(Ap​r​e​d,Ag​t)\mathcal{L}\_{a}=\text{MSE}(A\_{pred},A\_{gt}). The total loss for ego status is ℒe​g​o=ℒc​m​d+ℒv+ℒa\mathcal{L}\_{ego}=\mathcal{L}\_{cmd}+\mathcal{L}\_{v}+\mathcal{L}\_{a}. The final loss for end-to-end training is:

