#### 4.1.2 Training Configuration.

Latent-WMA is trained on 32 A100 GPUs for 100 epochs with a total batch size of 512, taking approximately two days. We employ the AdamW [loshchilov2019adamw] optimizer with a learning rate of 2×10−42\times 10^{-4} and weight decay 0.05. The training schedule incorporates linear warm-up over the first 10% steps, followed by cosine annealing scheduling to 1×10−61\times 10^{-6} after reaching the peak. BF16 mixed-precision training is applied to reduce memory footprint.

